# Loads the Nix devshell into the directory, so anything launched from here —
# VS Code, Metals, a plain terminal — sees the same JDK, sbt and Sail server.
#
# Without it, an editor started from Finder inherits none of that and Metals
# falls back to whatever JDK the system has, which for Spark 4 is the wrong one.
#
#     direnv allow
#
# Faster with nix-direnv (https://github.com/nix-community/nix-direnv), which
# caches the shell instead of rebuilding it on every cd.
# `use flake` watches flake.nix and flake.lock, but not versions.json — nix reads
# that one with builtins.readFile, a dependency direnv cannot see. Without this
# line the cached devshell keeps the old pysail interpolated inside it, and every
# activation reinstalls it: bump versions.json and the venv silently goes BACK to
# the previous release, leaving a new corpus pointed at an old binary. That is the
# exact mismatch docs/CORPUS.md warns about, and it is invisible.
watch_file versions.json

use flake
